00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.940
The US government and several legal and business groups filed briefs with the Supreme Court

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.720
urging reversal of at least part of the civil contempt ruling against Apple in the Epic

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.560
Games lawsuit.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.020
The District Court held Apple in contempt after the company allowed external purchase links

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.480
yet imposed a 27% commission on those transactions.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.680
Apple has since removed the commission entirely.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.760
The company maintains that the original injunction text did not prohibit charging a commission

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.980
and that lower courts improperly relied on the spirit of the order rather than its wording.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.760
The injunction states that Apple is permanently restrained from prohibiting developers from

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.540
including buttons, external links, or other calls to action that direct customers to purchasing

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.940
mechanisms outside in app purchasing.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:41.060
The Supreme Court agreed in late June to hear Apple's argument on this point.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.680
Google partnered with the Gates Foundation to direct $100 million toward organizations

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.940
that scale AI-powered climate and crop insights.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:56.520
The program targets 200 million smallholder farmers in Sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia,

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.440
and increase from the current 50 million reached.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:06.060
Smallholder farmers produce nearly 35% of the world's food across more than 500 million

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:12.100
